@defgroup micro-os-plus-micro-test-plus-operators Operators
@brief Deprecated overloaded operators for test comparisons.

@details
The overloaded operators `==`, `!=`, `<`, `>`, `<=`, `>=`, `and`, `or`, and
`not` are defined in the dedicated `micro_test_plus::operators` namespace,
to avoid conflicts with application-defined operators.

@par Deprecated
The operators are deprecated since 5.1.0, in favour of the function
comparators `mt::eq()`, `mt::ne()`, `mt::lt()`, `mt::le()`, `mt::gt()`, and
`mt::ge()`, and of the logical functions `mt::all_of()`, `mt::any_of()`, and
`mt::negate()`, which check and report the plain values, without literal
suffixes or casts. The compiler reports the use of the operators.

The operators are restricted to the framework types (see
`extension::is_op`). For constant values, this is achieved with the
(deprecated) literals, for example `1_i`, whilst dynamic values can be
wrapped with the (deprecated) converters such as `mt::to_i{expression}`.
When neither operand is of such a type, the standard operators are
selected; they return a plain `bool`, so a failed check cannot show the
operands.

@warning The overloaded `and` and `or` operators evaluate both operands
before the check, so they do not short-circuit like the built-in ones.

@par Replacement

@code{.cpp}
namespace mt = micro_os_plus::micro_test_plus;

ts.test ("Comparators", [] (auto& t) {
  t.expect (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42)) << "answer is 42";
  t.expect (mt::ne (compute_answer (), 43)) << "answer is not 43";
  t.expect (mt::lt (compute_answer (), 43)) << "answer is < 43";
  t.expect (mt::le (compute_answer (), 43)) << "answer is <= 43";
  t.expect (mt::gt (compute_answer (), 41)) << "answer is > 41";
  t.expect (mt::ge (compute_answer (), 42)) << "answer is >= 42";
  t.expect (mt::all_of (mt::eq (compute_answer (), 42),
                        mt::eq (compute_float (), 42.0f)));
});
@endcode
